LingTu changes (2026-10-30/31): C++ implementation over immutable OctoMap
columns, per-height bit-grid closing, separate inferred support storage,
occupied-height acceleration blocks and integration with native XYZ A*.
surface_graph.cpp and route_smoothing.cpp also adapt the fixed revision's
multi-source Voronoi corridors, string pulling and elastic-path update ideas
from nodes.rs, edges.rs, planner.rs and smoother.rs. The C++ adaptation uses
LingTu's 3D support, step/slope and cylinder checks, and retains native XYZ
search when a cached static corridor cannot serve current observations.
The Python/Rust bindings and Rust runtime dependencies are not included.

